      "writtenOn": "2026-09-22T12:27:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From my understanding of unrollInfo and `statement`, `statement` is the loopBody of the outer most loop, and thus does not automatically include the `unrollInfo-\u003efCount` information.\n\nso for example\n\n```C++\n    half4 main(half4 color) {\n        half4 x \u003d color;\n        for (int a \u003d 0; a \u003c 20; ++a) {          // Loop A (outer)\n            for (int b \u003d 0; b \u003c 20; ++b) {      // Loop B (inner)\n                x +\u003d half4(0.01);\n            }\n        }\n        return x;\n    }\n```\n\nWhen loop A gets passed to `loop_exceeds_nested_iteration_limit`, `statement` will contain the loop body of loop A (i.e. it will contain\n\n```C++\n            for (int b \u003d 0; b \u003c 20; ++b) {      // Loop B (inner)\n                x +\u003d half4(0.01);\n            }\n```\n\nSo we must set `fCurrentMultiplier` to `unrollInfo-\u003efCount` to account for the outer loop count.\n\n\nLet me know if there are any gaps in my understanding",
      "parentUuid": "bc972e84_3175d4ec",
